# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Working material, deliberately untracked rather than deleted.
#
# These are useful to *build* the submission and unpublishable *as* the
# submission: they carry the account locator, the escalation address, notes on
# the employer-IP boundary, and an assessment of other teams' repositories.
# They remain on disk (and are archived to ~/coco-archive) so the work can
# continue; git simply stops carrying them to a repository that goes public.
#
# Untracking does not rewrite history. The commits that already contain them
# are still reachable, which is why the go-public step squashes to a single
# orphan commit rather than relying on this file.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PRE_SUBMISSION.md
docs/research/
docs/submission_template/
docs/agent_onboarding_prompt.md
docs/notes_from_video_sessions.md
docs/SESSION_HANDOFF.md
docs/demo_runbook.md

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The public web viewer. Its secret is a private key, and this repository is
# public, so both the key and every local env file are excluded before the
# directory exists rather than after.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
web/node_modules/
web/.next/
web/out/
web/.vercel/
.env.local
.env*.local
*.p8
*.pem
web/*.tsbuildinfo
web/next-env.d.ts
